cosmic-client-toolkit: destroy the capture frame before reporting it

The portal's ready/failed handlers request the next frame (create_frame)
while the finished one still exists. cosmic-comp answers with a
duplicate_frame protocol error, the portal logs "wayland thread crash;
terminating", and the screen share freezes.

https://github.com/pop-os/xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic/issues/389
Applied to pop-os/cosmic-protocols by `sys portal patch` (see fish/docs.md).

diff --git a/client-toolkit/src/screencopy/dispatch.rs b/client-toolkit/src/screencopy/dispatch.rs
--- a/client-toolkit/src/screencopy/dispatch.rs
+++ b/client-toolkit/src/screencopy/dispatch.rs
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@ where
             }
             ext_image_copy_capture_frame_v1::Event::Ready => {
                 let frame = frame.lock().unwrap().clone();
+                screencopy_frame.destroy();
                 app_data.ready(
                     conn,
                     qh,
@@ -157,9 +158,9 @@ where
                     },
                     frame,
                 );
-                screencopy_frame.destroy();
             }
             ext_image_copy_capture_frame_v1::Event::Failed { reason } => {
+                screencopy_frame.destroy();
                 app_data.failed(
                     conn,
                     qh,
@@ -168,7 +169,6 @@ where
                     },
                     reason,
                 );
-                screencopy_frame.destroy();
             }
             _ => unreachable!(),
         }
